From: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/ttm/backup: use 0 instead of EMPTY_VMA_FLAGS

Same fix as ttm_tt.c but for the ttm_backup.c source.

Signed-off-by: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_backup.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_backup.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_backup.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_backup.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_backup.c
@@ -179,5 +179,9 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ttm_backup_bytes_avail);
 struct file *ttm_backup_shmem_create(loff_t size)
 {
+#ifdef BPM_EMPTY_VMA_FLAGS_NOT_PRESENT
+	return shmem_file_setup("ttm shmem backup", size, 0);
+#else
 	return shmem_file_setup("ttm shmem backup", size,
 				EMPTY_VMA_FLAGS);
+#endif
 }
-- 
2.34.1
